From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:34:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] phy: allwinner: a733-combophy: Add DisplayPort at 1.62 and
 5.4 Gb/s

The DisplayPort transmitter of the A733 runs its lanes at up to
5.4 Gb/s, and the combo PHY covers the DisplayPort rates RBR, HBR and
HBR2 (user manual sections 15.4.1 and 18.2.1). The PHY so far sets up
HBR only.

Add the PMA set-up and the swing and pre-emphasis settings of RBR and
HBR2. They differ from HBR in the PLL and clock settings, in the swing
and pre-emphasis tables, and at RBR in four more writes, one per lane.
HBR3 is not offered, as the PHY does not reach it.

The settings are vendor values, not measured on our boards. HBR2 needs
a sink that supports it, and training pattern 3, which the transmitter
chooses.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: not tested; the link to the test monitor
trained at the middle rate, so neither rate added here was used.

Assisted-by: LLM
